  "worked_solution": "The complement of $Q,$ denoted $\\overset{\u2015}{Q},$ consists of all the elements in $U$ that are not in $Q.$ To represent $\\overset{\u2015}{Q},$ we will shade in all the area of $U$ that is *outside* of $Q,$ as follows:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14035973/assets/c94ed2827be8a72e798295f16870b4873940f5dffe5b8e17786985a97ccbacb0.png)\n\nThe elements in the shaded area are $\u2663,\u2661,$ and $\u25b3.$ These are the elements of $U$ that are not in $Q.$ Therefore, the complement of $Q$ is\n\n$$\n\\overset{\u2015}{Q}={\u2663,\u2661,\u25b3}.\n$$",
